  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an integer array `nums`.\n\nYou replace each element in `nums` with the **sum** of its digits.\n\nOutput the **smallest** element in `nums` after all replacements.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [10,12,13,14]\n\n**Output:** 1\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n`nums` becomes `[1, 3, 4, 5]` after all replacements, with smallest element 1.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [1,2,3,4]\n\n**Output:** 1\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n`nums` becomes `[1, 2, 3, 4]` after all replacements, with smallest element 1.\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [999,19,199]\n\n**Output:** 10\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n`nums` becomes `[27, 10, 19]` after all replacements, with smallest element 10.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 100`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 104`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
